```


If I comment out `this.addEventListener(<x>, fn)`, then only a single one of each messages gets sent to the client, because the `this.#events.message` handler is enough to return a response. Alternatively, using `this.addEventListener` instead of `this.onmessage =` also fixes the issue.

Perhaps I am misusing the library, so this is a non-issue. But it is astonishing to me that this has not gotten reported in the three years since this code block was committed.

